Subject: [PATCH] guard the fallback GL typedefs behind SPOUT_NO_GL_TYPEDEFS
---
SpoutLibrary.h unconditionally re-declares `GLuint`/`GLenum` as `unsigned int` (and
`#define`s `GL_RGBA`) to avoid needing to include `GL.h`. A consumer that already has real
OpenGL type declarations in scope (e.g. glbinding's `gl::GLenum`, which is a scoped enum,
not a plain integer typedef) gets an ambiguous-symbol error merely from including this
header, and `GL_RGBA` there stops being usable as an enumerator name because it has become
a macro. Guard the fallback declarations so such a consumer can `#define
SPOUT_NO_GL_TYPEDEFS` before including this header and supply its own real GL types
instead.
Index: SPOUTSDK/SpoutLibrary/SpoutLibrary.h
===================================================================
--- a/SPOUTSDK/SpoutLibrary/SpoutLibrary.h
+++ b/SPOUTSDK/SpoutLibrary/SpoutLibrary.h
@@ -37,11 +37,13 @@
 #include <windows.h>
 #include <string>
 
+#ifndef SPOUT_NO_GL_TYPEDEFS
 // Re-define to avoid include of GL.h 
 typedef unsigned int GLuint;
 typedef unsigned int GLenum;
 #ifndef GL_RGBA
 #define GL_RGBA 0x1908
 #endif
+#endif // SPOUT_NO_GL_TYPEDEFS
 
 #define SPOUTLIBRARY_EXPORTS // defined for this DLL. The application imports rather than exports
